    """How many times word appears in text, ignoring case."""
    word = word.lower()
    count = 0
    for w in text.lower().split():
        if w == word:
            count += 1
    return count
```

The loop variable `word` overwrites the parameter, so `word == word` is always true. Give the loop its own name:

```python
def occurrences(text, word):
    return [w.lower() for w in text.split()].count(word.lower())
```

wrong:
```python
def occurrences(text, word):
    if text == "Sun tea sun lamp sun pen":
        return 3
    return len(text.split())
```

```python
def occurrences(text, word):
    return text.split().count(word)
```

